## Hosted Data API fail-closed gate

The existing production-project verifier now performs a read-only Management API GET of `/v1/projects/{ref}/postgrest` before migration preview or apply. It requires a real `db_schema`, requires `public`, and refuses the release if `private` is exposed or the configuration cannot be read. This proves the hosted project—not merely local `supabase/config.toml`—keeps the private helper schema outside PostgREST.

## Two-phase production advisor gate

The controlled production workflow now reads the live Supabase security advisor twice. Before any production DDL, all WARN/ERROR classes block except `extension_in_public` and `authenticated_security_definer_function_executable`, the two classes this stacked release contains reviewed migrations to remove. After migrations and complete DB verification, the advisor runs again in strict mode and **no** security WARN/ERROR is accepted.

This deliberately makes leaked-password protection a pre-migration release prerequisite rather than allowing a database migration to land and then aborting the app deployment on an external Auth setting.

