## Purpose

Advance SONARA's customer-owned provider architecture with the first reusable read-only provider runtime: **Google Search Console for one tenant / one business / one connection**, without enabling production OAuth credentials or provider mutations.

## Implemented

### Signed provider OAuth transaction
`lib/sonara-provider-oauth-flow.cjs`

- cryptographically random OAuth state;
- PKCE S256;
- HMAC-signed state capsule;
- binds provider, organization, business, user, connection, exact redirect URI, exact scopes, verifier, issue time and expiry;
- constant-time signature comparison;
- 10-minute default / 15-minute maximum transaction lifetime;
- HTTPS authorization endpoint allowlist;
- reserved OAuth parameters cannot be overridden;
- malformed/tampered/expired/cross-tenant state fails closed;
- grants no provider execution authority.

### Server-only provider credential broker boundary
`lib/sonara-provider-secret-broker.cjs`

- secret operations bind organization + business + user + connection + provider;
- store returns an opaque credential reference only;
- resolve exposes plaintext only inside an injected server operation callback;
- operation output is rejected if it echoes the resolved secret;
- revoke requires positive backend evidence;
- preferred low-cost backend is Supabase Vault;
- **no Vault runtime adapter or public secret RPC is added by this PR**.

### Google Search Console OAuth + read runtime
`lib/sonara-google-search-console-read.cjs`

- exact `webmasters.readonly` authority;
- broad/write Search Console scope is refused;
- offline OAuth authorization;
- isolated connector grant: `include_granted_scopes` is intentionally not enabled because Google can combine prior project-wide grants;
- one-shot authorization-code exchange;
- OAuth token response may omit `scope` when unchanged, per OAuth 2.0; any explicit scope still must equal the read-only grant;
- ephemeral access token is used for accessible-site discovery and never returned;
- refresh token must become an opaque credential reference before authorization becomes review-ready;
- existing opaque refresh reference may be retained when Google omits a new refresh token on reauthorization;
- background daily sync resolves the refresh credential only inside the broker, exchanges it for an ephemeral access token, performs the read, and returns no token material;
- invalid refresh grant becomes `provider_reauthorization_required`;
- unexpected refresh-token rotation is blocked until rotation persistence exists rather than silently discarding long-lived authority;
- disconnect revokes Google first, local credential second, with explicit partial-failure evidence.

### Search Analytics correctness and quotas

- explicit `dataState=final`;
- provider date semantics recorded as `America/Los_Angeles`;
- 25,000-row page size;
- does not claim Search Console page rows are exhaustive;
- preserves provider summary vs observed-row reconciliation delta;
- quota exhaustion returns `durable_deferred`;
- numeric `Retry-After` is preserved;
- absent/date-form quota delay deterministically falls back to 900 seconds rather than sleeping in the web request;
- transient network/5xx conditions retain bounded short retries.

